  ["Lock-in", "Low: apps are plain ABAP classes written against one interface, and the framework stays in your system", "SAP's programming model", "Low", "Screens live in the vendor's tables and run only on its runtime; leaving means rebuilding", "Apps live on the platform"],
  ["Source code", "Open, every line, on GitHub", "Closed", "UI5 open, your app yours", "Closed; some vendors export the generated app", "Closed"],
  ["Click-together designer", "None: an app is code, with hundreds of examples to start from and an AI builder that writes the class", "None: annotations, in ADT", "None: code", "Yes: drag-and-drop, templates, versions, for people who do not write code", "Yes", "even"],
