        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="plain two">
        {governance.map(([icon, h, t]) => <li><Icon name={icon} /><div><b>{h}</b><span>{t}</span></div></li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="callout"><b>No shadow IT.</b> No click-together designer bypasses your development process: every app is a class, under the rules you already have.</p>
      <p class="more">→ <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/review.md`}>The review pack</a>: everything a review board asks for, in one list, each line with the place that proves it. And in detail: <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/security`}>Security</a>, <a href={`${DOCS}configuration/authorization`}>Authorization</a>, the <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/security.md`}>security model</a>, <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/accessibility.md`}>Accessibility</a> and <a href={`${GITHUB}/blob/main/docs/verified-on.md`}>Verified on</a>.</p>
